  "original_source_bytes_preserved": true,
  "runtime_map_modified": false,
  "runtime_character_modified": false,
  "visual_review": "Continuing from `0fb8d78`, both hands retain unposed anatomical coordinates and joint landmarks. A separate editable shape key adds restrained knuckle, extensor-tendon and palm-crease relief while preserving the posed base surface. Ten curved nail plates are fitted through the source-to-posed surface correspondence, with fine thickness, keratin shading and a subtle free-edge tint. Permanent left/right hand inspection cameras expand the native review set to ten views.",
  "body_detail_review": "The first thumb footprint missed the tapered source surface. Adaptive fitting then exposed rough thumbnail edges in underside renders, so the retained revision stays on facing surface regions, uses denser plate samples and greater surface clearance. Front and palm studies were reviewed on both hands. The verifier checks the connected hand surfaces, retained shape keys, ten individually identified plates, every nail vertex and face center against the posed skin, and closed outward nail thickness. The retained maximum hand relief is about 0.80 mm and minimum sampled nail clearance about 0.14 mm. Passing these checks does not establish human realism.",
  "remaining": "The full realism goal remains active. The hands have more definition but still need finer skin/cuticle quality; the face remains generic, and the jacket folds remain too soft in places. Next develop facial individuality and broader skin variation, then reassess the whole character and garment folds against the original reference. Architecture/retail variety and planting realism follow human acceptance. This remains an editable offline Blender study, with static fitted nails rather than an animation rig or runtime update.",
